-- ============================================================================
-- crude PROFESSIONAL DEEP SEED: Crude Assay & Blending, intermediate tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: THE BLENDED BARREL AND WHAT IT IS WORTH. Yields add on
-- volume, so the blend has its own curve at every temperature a crude
-- measured, and temperatures are never averaged; T50 is read off that curve
-- by interpolation; a refinery draws its own cut points and a moved cut point
-- moves barrels between two cuts only; the netback takes losses on the product
-- side before processing and freight, names a blank cost and an unpriced cut,
-- and reports its differential against a marker.
--
-- THE ENGINE FACT THIS TIER OWNS. The blend is worth what its barrels are
-- worth: its netback and the volume-weighted netbacks of its crudes are the
-- same figure.
--
-- THE TRAP THE TIER IS BUILT ON. A grid reading of T50, a mass-weighted yield
-- and a loss taken after the costs each give a figure that looks finished.
--
-- HELD, taught as a limit and never graded: Watson K taken at T50 (C13).
-- Every figure is invented and illustrative. The capstone grades six
-- four-decimal engine figures at a tolerance of 5e-5.
-- ============================================================================

values ('crude', 'intermediate', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-the-blends-own-curve","title":"The Blend''s Own Curve","lesson_keys":["l01-yields-add-on-volume","l02-temperatures-do-not-average","l03-every-temperature-a-crude-measured","l04-a-truncated-crude-in-the-blend"]},{"key":"m02-the-fifty-percent-point","title":"The Fifty Percent Point","lesson_keys":["l01-reading-a-temperature-off-the-curve","l02-interpolated-against-the-grid","l03-the-component-midpoints-do-not-average","l04-the-watson-factor","l05-a-screening-basis-for-k"]},{"key":"m03-cut-yields-of-the-blend","title":"Cut Yields of the Blend","lesson_keys":["l01-the-blends-cut-yields","l02-moving-a-cut-point","l03-a-cut-the-curve-cannot-answer","l04-the-refinery-draws-its-own-cuts"]},{"key":"m04-netback","title":"Netback","lesson_keys":["l01-product-value-per-barrel-of-crude","l02-losses-on-the-product-side","l03-processing-and-freight","l04-a-blank-cost-is-named","l05-an-unpriced-cut"]},{"key":"m05-against-the-marker","title":"Against the Marker","lesson_keys":["l01-the-differential","l02-each-crude-on-its-own-netback","l03-the-blend-against-its-components","l04-losses-outside-zero-to-one-hundred","l05-d86-is-a-product-test"]},{"key":"m06-the-professional-reading","title":"The Professional Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-kwale-valuation-end-to-end","l02-what-the-oracle-checks-on-a-cargo","l03-what-the-next-tier-changes"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
